## Import

{{ codefile "shell" .ImportFile }}

Import populates `gid`, and `members` if the group has any. `system` cannot be determined from `/etc/group`, so it is left unset; setting it in the configuration afterwards updates the state in place without recreating the group.

## Caveats

- Requires root privileges.
- Deleting a group fails while it is the primary group of an existing user. Reference the group from `sysutils_user.gid` so Terraform orders the operations correctly.
- Do not manage the same membership from both `sysutils_group.members` and `sysutils_user.groups`; the two resources would keep overwriting each other. Pick one side.
- Only the local files (`/etc/group`, `/etc/gshadow`) are managed; groups provided by LDAP, SSSD or NIS are invisible to this resource.
